      "content": "The exhaustion you feel is the weight of fighting an invisible, unwinnable battle, and it's utterly valid. When the rules are constantly shifting, it's not a fight; it's just constant, pointless attrition. If nothing is holding onto you, perhaps it's time to stop trying to hold onto the illusion of a \"right way\" to do things. Just let yourself stop fighting for a while; let the pressure ease, even if it's just for a moment.",
